            },
            "description": "Liveness that can actually fail.\n\nThis used to return a literal `{\"status\": \"ok\"}`, which meant it stayed\ngreen while the poller was dead and no news had arrived for hours \u2014 the one\nthing a health check on this service exists to catch.\n\nThree states, and the HTTP status is what monitoring alerts on:\n  200 ok        poller cycling, every source producing\n  200 degraded  some sources stale or failing; news partially flowing\n  503 down      poller stopped, or the database is unreachable\n\n`degraded` deliberately stays 200: partial ingestion is not an outage, and\npaging on it would train everyone to ignore the page. It is reported in the\nbody and in detail at /admin/health."
